# Understanding the difference between .zprofile and .zshrc:
#  .zprofile: This file is executed only once when you log in to a new shell session. 
#             It's ideal for setting environment variables that need to be set only once per login.
#  .zshrc:    This file is executed every time you open a new terminal window or tab. It's suitable 
#             for setting environment variables or aliases that need to be applied to each new shell instance.


